# oracle: pppm/dielectric with fix polarize/functional (confined: two ions between two dielectric interfaces, PPPM/dielectric; examples/PACKAGES/dielectric in.confined.dof; cut-down: the interface atoms with x >= 20 are removed from both walls (w71diel_confined_half.data: 2002 atoms instead of 4002), because the functional's Rww matrix is built over all interface atoms (N^2 memory and work: 16 s for 4000 atoms))
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): G 0.24260797 and grid 12 12 36 match; the engine agrees to 3.2e-9 relative (elong, row 0) and 4.8e-13 per atom (fz) for the half-wall data; the functional CG solve is iterative (tol 1e-4).
# oracle-inputs: w71diel_confined_half.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
atom_style      dielectric
atom_modify     map array
dimension       3
boundary        p p f
read_data       w71diel_confined_half.data
group interface type 1
group ions type 2 3
group cations type 2
group anions type 3
set group cations epsilon 10
set group anions epsilon 10
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/long/dielectric 1.122 10.0
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff      1 1 0.0 1.0
kspace_style    pppm/dielectric 0.0001
kspace_modify   slab 3.0
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes one 5000
fix             1 ions nve
fix             3 interface polarize/functional 1 0.0001
fix_modify      3 dielectrics -10 15 1.0 0.866 NULL
thermo          1000
thermo_style    custom step evdwl ecoul elong epair
thermo_modify   flush yes format float %.15g
run             0
